PART 2 — WORDPRESS BACKUPS (Cloudways → R2)
SCOPE

Per-site only

No Cloudflare Workers involved

Runs on VPS via cron

Designed for reliability and restore speed

WHAT TO BACK UP

For each WordPress site:

Database

wp-content/ (themes, plugins, uploads)

Exclude:

WordPress core

cache directories

logs

BACKUP SCRIPT REQUIREMENTS
Script name

pg-backup-wp.sh

Inputs (env vars or arguments)
SITE_NAME
APP_PATH
DB_NAME
DB_USER
DB_PASS
DB_HOST
R2_BUCKET
R2_PREFIX

Steps (STRICT ORDER)

Create temp working directory

Dump DB:

mysqldump --single-transaction --quick
gzip output


Archive wp-content:

tar --exclude=cache
gzip


Upload both files to Cloudflare R2

Use rclone OR aws s3 compatible API

Verify upload success

Delete temp files

Exit with non-zero on failure

FILE NAMING CONVENTION
{site-name}/
  ├── db/
  │   └── site-db-YYYY-MM-DD.sql.gz
  └── files/
      └── wp-content-YYYY-MM-DD.tar.gz

R2 CONFIG

Use S3-compatible API

Credentials stored in:

~/.aws/credentials

OR environment variables

OPTIONAL: BACKUP HEARTBEAT

After successful backup:

POST https://uptime.yourdomain.com/backup-heartbeat
Payload:

{
  "site": "example.com",
  "status": "success",
  "timestamp": "ISO8601"
}


Used to alert if backups stop running.

RESTORE NOTES (DOCUMENTED BUT NOT AUTOMATED)

