AUTHENTICATION (Cloudflare Access)

No auth code in the application

Configured in Cloudflare dashboard:
1. Create Access Application for your Worker domain
2. Add Access Policy (allow specific emails)
3. Choose identity provider (email OTP, Google, GitHub, etc.)

Cloudflare Access handles:
- Login page
- Session management
- JWT validation

Worker receives authenticated user in CF-Access-Authenticated-User-Email header

Setup steps (post-deploy):
1. Go to Cloudflare Zero Trust dashboard
2. Create Application → Self-hosted
3. Set application domain to your Worker URL
4. Add policy: Allow → Emails ending in @yourdomain.com
5. Done — all requests now require auth

